#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD9723 expect=violation domain=SE
#note "The sister half of the FDA-SD0092 pair (minted 2026-09-11, M10/T1-37), serving FDA-SD0092 and FDA-SD1266 (one sister per target variable and package - identical 10-package sets). SEUPDES is not in the dataset (None satisfied) while rows 2 and 3 code ETCD='UNPLAN', so the remaining condition holds on two rows. Sensitivity is Dataset, so the absence is reported ONCE although both rows qualify. Same dataset shape as the parents' skipped_no_seupdes_column scenarios: the parents skip, this rule reports."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
dataset SE label="Subject Elements"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col SESEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col ETCD    type=Char label="Element Code"
col ELEMENT type=Char label="Description of Element"
---
S1 | SE | 001 | 1 | SCRN   | Screening
S1 | SE | 001 | 2 | UNPLAN | Unplanned Element
S1 | SE | 002 | 1 | UNPLAN | Unplanned Element
